{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489065-vtm-but-with-only-common-disciplines","id":1489065,"title":"VTM but with only common disciplines?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-04T00:24:29-07:00","id":1489065,"title":"VTM but with only common disciplines?","content":"I've always liked the 8 &quot;common&quot; disciplines, as they represent the classic vampire powers, at least based on a Dracula archetype. Through them the vampire can achieve a superhuman body (the physical disciplines), enhanced senses to the point of ESP (Auspex), control over all creatures (Dominate, Presence, Obfuscate, Animalism) and shapeshifting (Protean). How would you rework the clans for a game with only these disciplines to choose from? Most of the camarilla clans already have this, but would you change the current spreads?<br /> <br /> V20 rules, as V5 is basically this + blood sorcery and oblivion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27522-yamio","user":"Yamio","date":". 08-04-2022, 03:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27522-yamio","name":"Yamio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T06:37:51-07:00","id":1489103,"title":"","content":"What would be the benefit? It might work really well if you went -Caitiff only- but that would cut away a lot of the interesting clan dynamics. The clans that aren't in the Camarilla are largely not in it because they're extremes that either directly go against the status quo (Assamites, Ravnos) or they would invite hostility to the status quo (FoS, Gio). Disciplines are a big part of the character of clans and getting rid of the unique disciplines would largely erode the idea that the clan is extreme. For instance, Tzmisce without Vicissitude don't have any good reason to batter their own humanity with inhumane experiments on animals and people. Tzmisce without Vicissitude can't give criminals new faces and identities, Tzmisce without Vicissitude aren't making mishappen monsters: Tzmisce experiments are a large part of why the clan has developed a culture with so much emphasis on hospitality: &quot;welcome to my haven, you can do whatever you want, but if you go into that room there, I'm adding you to my menagerie&quot;. In simple, you take Vicissitude from Tzmisce, they're nothing more than a mild deviation from another clan (depending on what you replace Vicissitude with) and there's no reason to keep them at arms length with the Cam as they're <i>just another clan with nothing wrong with them. </i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also<br /> I really, really like Thaumaturgy, especially my own little twist for it. I realise that's not a universal opinion as many threads have been made on getting rid of it, but for me it's very much a -the more you know, the more you like it- power. I can do without Assamites, FoS, Tzmisce or Ravnos, much as I love them all; but without vampire wizards and witches, what's the point?<br /> <br /> A tightly focused game with only a few clans in the picture? Sure. But to do this to the whole setting? That's a paddling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T06:52:29-07:00","id":1489106,"title":"","content":"Rather than reworking everything, I would just play Kindred of the East. You pick your disciplines rather than being locked into them by clan choice, and there are equivalents to all the basic V:tM Disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T07:45:17-07:00","id":1489111,"title":"","content":"I would od it something like this. In the order that they came to mind.<br /> <br /> Brujah - As before<br /> <br /> Gangrel - As before<br /> <br /> Assamite - Add Potence<br /> <br /> Giovanni - Add Auspex<br /> <br /> Ventrue - As before<br /> <br /> Toreador - As before<br /> <br /> Tremere - Add Fortitude<br /> <br /> Nosferatu - As before<br /> <br /> Ravnos - Add Presence<br /> <br /> Malkavians - As before with Dominate<br /> <br /> Lasombra - Add Obfuscate<br /> <br /> Tzimisce - Add Protean<br /> <br /> Setites - Add Auspex<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T11:59:01-07:00","id":1489142,"title":"","content":"My take on the topic would be the following.<br /> <br /> The Brujah, Ventrue, Torador, Malkavians, Gangrel and Nosferatu would have the same discipline spread as before.<br /> <br /> Assamite, and Tremere I would add Forititude to them<br /> <br /> Tzimisce I would add Protean to the mix since Blood Sorcery isn't common.<br /> <br /> Giovanni, Followers Of Set and Ravnos I would add Auspex<br /> <br /> The Lasombra I would add Obfuscate to them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T16:29:30-07:00","id":1489164,"title":"","content":"Removing the specialty Disciplines for the other clans, this is what I would do:<br /> <br /> Tremere - Animalism<br /> Lasombra - Obfuscate<br /> Tzimisce - Protean<br /> Assamites - Fortitude<br /> Cappadocians - Potence<br /> Followers of Set - Protean<br /> Ravnos (See below)<br /> <br /> My original idea was at first to replace the signature Discipline with its thematic counterpart. But then I compared how often each individual Discipline was In-Clan, and saw there was an imbalance among the Disciplines. Some were far more common than others. I wanted to keep each of them around 4-5 clans that had them in-clan. So I had to make some changes.<br /> <br /> I was not happen with how the Ravnos turned out. Instead of just making one change, I now want to redo their Disciplines entirely to make sure they are not close to other Clans. I'd probably give them Animalism, Celerity, Presence.<br /> <br /> That keeps every Discipline at 4-5 clans having it in-clan, except for Protean which only has 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}